 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nAuthorization and token response methods have incorrect parameter order\n\n#### Description\n\nThe OpenID Connect grant dispatchers are passing parameters in the wrong order to their handler methods, causing authorization and token creation to fail.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.openid.connect.core.endpoints import Server\nfrom oauthlib.openid.connect.core.grant_types import AuthorizationCodeGrant\n\n# Set up a basic OpenID Connect server\nserver = Server()\n\n# Try to create an authorization response\nuri = 'http://example.com/path?client_id=abc&scope=openid&response_type=code'\ntry:\n    headers, body, status = server.create_authorization_response(uri, scopes='openid')\n    print(\"Authorization response created successfully\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error creating authorization response: {e}\")\n\n# Try to create a token response  \ntoken_uri = 'http://example.com/path'\ntoken_body = 'client_id=me&redirect_uri=http://back.to/me&grant_type=authorization_code&code=test_code'\ntry:\n    headers, body, status = server.create_token_response(token_uri, body=token_body)\n    print(\"Token response created successfully\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error creating token response: {e}\")\n```\n\nThe methods fail because the dispatcher is passing `token_handler` and `request` parameters in the wrong order to the underlying grant handlers.\n</issue>\n",
